drm/vc4: stop output polling when the driver unbinds

Faraday's own change, not from mainline.

vc4_kms_load calls drm_kms_helper_poll_init, which queues the output
poll's delayed work 10 s ahead, and nothing in vc4 calls
drm_kms_helper_poll_fini. Unbinding the driver frees the DRM device
that holds that work while its timer is still pending. The timer then
fires from freed memory and the kernel panics in a timer softirq with a
bad PC.

The Pi's boot unbinds and binds vc4 again to bring up a DPI panel, so a
Pi with the 2.8-inch panel panicked about 13 s after power-on. HDMI's
route does not unbind.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_drv.c
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@
 #include <drm/drm_atomic_helper.h>
 #include <drm/drm_drv.h>
 #include <drm/drm_fb_helper.h>
+#include <drm/drm_probe_helper.h>
 #include <drm/drm_vblank.h>
 
 #include <soc/bcm2835/raspberrypi-firmware.h>
@@ -428,6 +429,7 @@
 {
 	struct drm_device *drm = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
+	drm_kms_helper_poll_fini(drm);
 	drm_dev_unplug(drm);
 	drm_atomic_helper_shutdown(drm);
 }
